 Hum Genet 9:849&#x02013;857. doi:10.1375/twin.9.6.849 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17254420</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bouchard</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic and environmental influences on adult intelligence and special mental abilities</article-title><source>Hum Biol</source><year>1998</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>279</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bouchard TJ Jr (1998) Genetic and environmental influences on adult intelligence and special mental abilities. Hum Biol 70:257&#x02013;279 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9549239</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bouchard</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Malina</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetics of physiological fitness and motor performance</article-title><source>Exerc Sport Sci Rev</source><year>1983</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>306</fpage><lpage>339</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1249/00003677-198301000-00011</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bouchard C, Malina RM (1983) Genetics of physiological fitness and motor performance. Exerc Sport Sci Rev 11:306&#x02013;339. doi:10.1249/00003677-198301000-00011 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6350021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bouchard</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lykken</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name><name><surname>McGue</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Segal</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Tellegen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sources of human psychological differences: the Minnesota study of twins reared apart</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1990</year><volume>250</volume><fpage>223</fpage><lpage>228</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.2218526</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bouchard TJ Jr, Lykken DT, McGue M, Segal NL, Tellegen A (1990) Sources of human psychological differences: the Minnesota study of twins reared apart. Science 250:223&#x02013;228. doi:10.1126/science.2218526 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2218526</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Engelman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Frane</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jennrich</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Toporek</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><source>Frequency tables. In BMDP STATISTICAL SOFTWARE</source><year>1983</year><publisher-loc>Berkeley</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of California Press</publisher-name><fpage>155</fpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Brown MB, Engelman L, Frane JW, Hill MA, Jennrich RI, Toporek JD (1983) Frequency tables. In BMDP STATISTICAL SOFTWARE. University of California Press, Berkeley, p 155 </citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carey</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Twin imitation for antisocial behavior: implications for genetic and family environment research</article-title><source>J Abnorm Psychol</source><year>1992</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0021-843X.101.1.18</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Carey G (1992) Twin imitation for antisocial behavior: implications for genetic and family environment research. J Abnorm Psychol 101:18&#x02013;25. doi:10.1037/0021-843X.101.1.18 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1537964</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><citation citation-type="other">Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek (2009) Den Haag/Heerlen</citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coon</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Carey</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic and environmental determinants of musical ability in twins</article-title><source>Behav Genet</source><year>1989</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>193</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF01065903</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Coon H, Carey G (1989) Genetic and environmental determinants of musical ability in twins. Behav Genet 19:183&#x02013;193. doi:10.1007/BF01065903 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2719622</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruin</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Rikers</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The influence of achievement motivation and chess-specific motivation on deliberate practice</article-title><source>J Sport Exerc Psychol</source><year>2007</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>561</fpage><lpage>583</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">De Bruin AB, Rikers RM, Schmidt HG (2007) The influence of achievement motivation and chess-specific motivation on deliberate practice. J Sport Exerc Psychol 29:561&#x02013;583 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18089893</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruin</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Smits</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Rikers</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Deliberate practice predicts performance over time in adolescent chess players and drop-outs: a linear mixed models analysis</article-title><source>Br J Psychol</source><year>2008</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>497</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1348/000712608X295631</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">De Bruin AB, Smits N, Rikers RM, Schmidt HG (2008) Deliberate practice predicts performance over time in adolescent chess players and drop-outs: a linear mixed models analysis. Br J Psychol 99:473&#x02013;497. doi:10.1348/000712608X295631 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18433518</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moor</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Spector</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Cherkas</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Falchi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hottenga</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Boomsma</surname><given-names>DI</given-names></name><name><surname>Geus</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genome-wide linkage scan for athlete status in 700 British female DZ twin pairs</article-title><source>Twin Res Hum Genet</source><year>2007</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>812</fpage><lpage>820</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1375/twin.10.6.812</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">De Moor MH, Spector TD, Cherkas LF, Falchi M, Hottenga JJ, Bo